import{_ as e,o as a,c as o,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.il0noOp3.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"FinOps Review — enumerated source for the FinOps Review assessment","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"frameworks/finops-review-question-set.md","filePath":"frameworks/finops-review-question-set.md"}'),n={name:"frameworks/finops-review-question-set.md"};function s(r,t,d,c,l,u){return a(),o("div",null,[...t[0]||(t[0]=[i('<h1 id="finops-review-—-enumerated-source-for-the-finops-review-assessment" tabindex="-1">FinOps Review — enumerated source for the FinOps Review assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#finops-review-—-enumerated-source-for-the-finops-review-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;FinOps Review — enumerated source for the FinOps Review assessment&quot;">​</a></h1><p><strong>Enumerated 2026-08-01; re-verified and aligned to the FinOps Framework 2026 on 2026-11-24. Verification method and limits are stated below — read them before quoting any coverage number from this page.</strong></p><p><strong>Framework version:</strong> FinOps Framework 2026 (FinOps Foundation, 2026-03-20 update; 4 domains / 22 capabilities) per Microsoft FinOps Review (New) <code>60c02533-b280-4dec-ac5f-3f10cdd238b9</code>, verified 2026-11-24. Microsoft does not number the assessment itself; the verification date above is the version, per <code>docs/frameworks/README.md</code>. Re-date this line when this file is next re-verified.</p><p>This is the AB#6814 enumeration for target #9 in the audit&#39;s fourteen-assessment programme (<code>pmo/audits/AZURE-SCOUT-AUDIT.md</code> §14): <em>&quot;FinOps Review — Cost surface exists … <code>waf.cost</code> (6 rules) + <code>caf.billing</code> (misnamed, holds cost rules).&quot;</em> Neither existing file scores against the FinOps Framework itself — they score WAF&#39;s Cost Optimization pillar and (mislabelled) cost-cleanup rules respectively. Per DQ12, no FinOps-Framework-shaped rule file is written until this enumeration exists.</p><h2 id="what-the-finops-review-is" tabindex="-1">What the FinOps Review is <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-the-finops-review-is" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What the FinOps Review is&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The <strong>FinOps Review</strong> is an interactive assessment on the Microsoft Assessments platform, multiple-choice/multiple-response, described as <em>&quot;a lightweight, self-guided assessment&quot;</em> to <em>&quot;identify capability gaps.&quot;</em> It is published under two assessment ids, and as of 2026-11-24 <strong>both render the same &quot;FinOps Review (New)&quot; page</strong>:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Assessment id</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>60c02533-b280-4dec-ac5f-3f10cdd238b9</code></td><td>The current &quot;FinOps Review (New)&quot; — <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/assessments/60c02533-b280-4dec-ac5f-3f10cdd238b9/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/assessments/60c02533-b280-4dec-ac5f-3f10cdd238b9/</a>. This is the id Scout cites.</td></tr><tr><td><code>ad1c0f6b-396b-44a4-924b-7a4c778a13d3</code></td><td>The original FinOps Review id (<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/assessments/ad1c0f6b-396b-44a4-924b-7a4c778a13d3" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/assessments/ad1c0f6b-396b-44a4-924b-7a4c778a13d3</a>). It now renders the same &quot;(New)&quot; page, so it is an alias, not a separate assessment.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Its subject is the <strong>FinOps Framework</strong> from the FinOps Foundation. Microsoft publishes the framework on Learn (<a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/finops-framework" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/finops-framework</a>, capability list at <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/capabilities" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/capabilities</a>). The framework organises <strong>22 capabilities</strong> into 4 domains — 3 operational domains (Understand usage and cost, Quantify business value, Optimize usage and cost) plus one practice-management domain (Manage the FinOps practice). This enumeration is built from that published capability list, using the 2026 capability names.</p><h2 id="what-changed-in-the-finops-framework-2025-and-2026" tabindex="-1">What changed in the FinOps Framework (2025 and 2026) <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-changed-in-the-finops-framework-2025-and-2026" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What changed in the FinOps Framework (2025 and 2026)&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The FinOps Foundation updates the framework each March (<a href="https://www.finops.org/insights/2026-finops-framework/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.finops.org/insights/2026-finops-framework/</a>):</p><ul><li><strong>2025-03-20 update:</strong> added the <strong>Scopes</strong> construct (how the framework is applied to a defined part of the estate or organisation) and renamed &quot;Cloud Policy &amp; Governance&quot; to &quot;Policy &amp; Governance&quot;.</li><li><strong>2026-03-20 update:</strong> renamed several capabilities (table below) and added the <strong>Executive Strategy Alignment</strong> capability. The framework is still 4 domains / 22 capabilities, because Onboarding Workloads no longer appears in the Foundation&#39;s list (its Foundation page returns 404).</li><li><strong>Microsoft Learn lag:</strong> the Learn capability list at the URL above still lists Onboarding Workloads and does not yet list Executive Strategy Alignment.</li></ul><p>Scout resolves the mismatch by keeping both: <strong>23 rules</strong> — the 22 capabilities Microsoft Learn lists (Onboarding Workloads kept, labelled as no longer in the Foundation 2026 list) plus <code>FINOPS-M09</code> Executive Strategy Alignment. Rule ids are unchanged by the renames, so existing questionnaire answer files keep working.</p><h3 id="capability-rename-map" tabindex="-1">Capability rename map <a class="header-anchor" href="#capability-rename-map" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Capability rename map&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Rule id</th><th>Previous name (Scout enumeration / earlier framework)</th><th>2026 name (used in rule titles)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FINOPS-Q04</td><td>Benchmarking</td><td><strong>KPIs &amp; Benchmarking</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O01</td><td>Architecting for the cloud</td><td><strong>Architecting &amp; Workload Placement</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O02</td><td>Workload optimization</td><td><strong>Usage Optimization</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O05</td><td>Cloud sustainability</td><td><strong>Sustainability</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M04</td><td>Policy and governance</td><td><strong>Governance, Policy &amp; Risk</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M07</td><td>FinOps tools and services</td><td><strong>Automation, Tools &amp; Services</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M08</td><td>Intersecting frameworks</td><td><strong>Intersecting Disciplines</strong></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M03</td><td>Onboarding workloads</td><td>Unchanged name, but <strong>a Microsoft Learn capability no longer in the FinOps Foundation 2026 list</strong> — kept and labelled</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M09</td><td>(did not exist)</td><td><strong>Executive Strategy Alignment</strong> — new in 2026</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Unchanged capabilities: Data ingestion (U01), Allocation (U02), Reporting &amp; analytics (U03), Anomaly management (U04), Planning &amp; estimating (Q01), Forecasting (Q02), Budgeting (Q03), Unit economics (Q05), Rate optimization (O03), Licensing &amp; SaaS (O04), FinOps education &amp; enablement (M01), FinOps practice operations (M02), Invoicing &amp; chargeback (M05), FinOps assessment (M06).</p><h2 id="verification-method-—-and-the-one-thing-this-enumeration-is-not" tabindex="-1">Verification method — and the one thing this enumeration is NOT <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-method-—-and-the-one-thing-this-enumeration-is-not" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification method — and the one thing this enumeration is NOT&quot;">​</a></h2><p><strong>What was read (2026-08-01, re-checked 2026-11-24):</strong></p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Source</th><th>What it gave</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>The FinOps Review (New) assessment landing page (<code>60c02533-…</code>)</td><td>Confirms the assessment exists, its duration/format, and that it is self-guided against the FinOps Framework. <strong>No question text.</strong></td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://www.finops.org/insights/2026-finops-framework/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FinOps Foundation 2026 framework update</a></td><td>The 2026 capability renames and the new Executive Strategy Alignment capability</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/capabilities" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">FinOps capabilities</a></td><td>The Microsoft Learn 22-capability, 4-domain structure (still lists Onboarding Workloads)</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/optimize/optimize-cloud-usage-cost" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Optimize usage and cost</a></td><td>Per-capability definitions for the Optimize domain</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/cloud-computing/finops/framework/quantify/quantify-business-value" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Quantify business value</a></td><td>Per-capability definitions for the Quantify domain</td></tr><tr><td><code>src/collect/Get-ScoutCostInventory.ps1</code>, <code>src/analyze/Get-ScoutCostAnomaly.ps1</code></td><td>Ground truth for what cost data Scout actually collects and computes, versus what is merely available as an unused function — read directly, not inferred from the audit</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>⚠️ The assessment&#39;s own question TEXT and NUMBERS are not published.</strong> Microsoft publishes no question text for the New review either. The <code>FINOPS-*</code> identifiers and the question wording below are <strong>Scout&#39;s own inference</strong> from the published framework&#39;s capability names — Microsoft attributes the framework itself to the FinOps Foundation, not to the assessment. A Scout score against this file is not a Microsoft FinOps Review score.</p><p><strong>Shelf life.</strong> The FinOps Framework updates every March and the FinOps toolkit ships monthly releases (see the toolkit&#39;s own roadmap page); re-verify before quoting.</p><h2 id="the-enumeration" tabindex="-1">The enumeration <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-enumeration" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The enumeration&quot;">​</a></h2><h3 id="understand-usage-and-cost" tabindex="-1">Understand usage and cost <a class="header-anchor" href="#understand-usage-and-cost" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Understand usage and cost&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Scout can evidence?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FINOPS-U01</td><td>Cost and usage data is ingested from the cloud provider (and ideally other sources) into a single accessible repository</td><td>⚠️ Partial — <code>src/collect/Get-ScoutCostInventory.ps1</code> (per-subscription cost grouped by type/resource group/location/service) exists but is <strong>opt-in</strong>: it requires <code>Az.CostManagement</code>, which is deliberately excluded from Scout&#39;s core manifest dependencies because installing it can force an incompatible <code>Az.Accounts</code> upgrade. No non-Azure source is ever ingested.</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-U02</td><td>Cost is allocated meaningfully — broken down by tag, resource group, or business unit</td><td>⚠️ Partial — cost is grouped by resource group/location/service/type per subscription; that grouping is not joined to <code>$.tags[*]</code>, so tag-based allocation is not currently possible from the same dataset</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-U03</td><td>Cost and usage data is reported on and made visible to stakeholders</td><td>⚠️ Partial — a &quot;Costs&quot; worksheet is produced via <code>Start-AZTIExtractionOrchestration.ps1</code>, but that call path is separate from the unified <code>-Assessment</code> entry point&#39;s <code>collect.json</code>, so no rule can currently query it</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-U04</td><td>Anomalies (spikes, unexpected changes) are proactively identified and reacted to</td><td>⚠️ Partial — <code>src/analyze/Get-ScoutCostAnomaly.ps1</code> implements three independent detection techniques (spike, z-score, IQR) against <code>Get-ScoutCostInventory</code> output, wired into the collect pipeline (AB#6826)</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="quantify-business-value" tabindex="-1">Quantify business value <a class="header-anchor" href="#quantify-business-value" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Quantify business value&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Scout can evidence?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FINOPS-Q01</td><td>Cost and usage of new or changing workloads is predicted before deployment</td><td>❌ Not collected — no pre-deployment cost-estimation data source</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-Q02</td><td>Future cost is forecast from historical trends</td><td>✅ <code>Management/Budgets</code> (&quot;Forecast Spend&quot; field)</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-Q03</td><td>Budgets are actively monitored and managed, with alerts configured</td><td>✅ <code>Management/Budgets</code> (&quot;Amount&quot;, &quot;Current Spend&quot;, &quot;Budget Used %&quot;, &quot;Alerts Configured&quot;)</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-Q04</td><td><strong>KPIs &amp; Benchmarking</strong> — cloud efficiency is measured with KPIs and benchmarked against internal teams or industry peers</td><td>❌ Not collected — no KPI or benchmarking dataset</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-Q05</td><td>Unit economics (cost per business unit of value) are calculated</td><td>❌ Not collected — requires business-metric data outside Azure&#39;s control plane</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="optimize-usage-and-cost" tabindex="-1">Optimize usage and cost <a class="header-anchor" href="#optimize-usage-and-cost" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Optimize usage and cost&quot;">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Scout can evidence?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FINOPS-O01</td><td><strong>Architecting &amp; Workload Placement</strong> — cloud solutions are architected for cost efficiency and placed deliberately during design/migration, not retrofitted after deployment</td><td>❌ Design-time decision, not observable post-deployment</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O02</td><td><strong>Usage Optimization</strong> — workload cost/usage is analyzed to identify efficiency opportunities</td><td>✅ <code>$.advisor[?(@.Category == &#39;Cost&#39;)]</code>, <code>$.costCleanup.orphanedDisks[*]</code>, <code>$.costCleanup.orphanedPips[*]</code></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O03</td><td>Rate optimization is pursued — reservations, savings plans, commitment-discount planning</td><td>✅ <code>General/Reservations</code>, <code>General/ReservationRecom</code></td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O04</td><td>Software licenses and prepaid SaaS products (including Azure Hybrid Benefit) are tracked and fully utilized</td><td>✅ Windows VMs without Azure Hybrid Benefit (<code>$.compute.virtualMachines</code> <code>licenseType</code>)</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-O05</td><td><strong>Sustainability</strong> — carbon emissions are measured alongside cost as part of cloud sustainability</td><td>❌ Not collected — Scout has no Emissions/Carbon API collector</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="manage-the-finops-practice" tabindex="-1">Manage the FinOps practice <a class="header-anchor" href="#manage-the-finops-practice" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Manage the FinOps practice&quot;">​</a></h3><p>This domain is almost entirely organisational — it describes running and maturing the FinOps practice itself, not the resources it manages.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>#</th><th>Item</th><th>Scout can evidence?</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>FINOPS-M01</td><td>A FinOps education and enablement programme exists</td><td>❌ Organisational</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M02</td><td>FinOps practice operations (cadence, ownership, processes) are defined</td><td>❌ Organisational</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M03</td><td><strong>Onboarding Workloads</strong> — workloads are onboarded to the FinOps practice based on financial/technical feasibility. <em>Microsoft Learn capability, no longer in the FinOps Foundation 2026 list.</em></td><td>❌ Organisational</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M04</td><td><strong>Governance, Policy &amp; Risk</strong> — FinOps-specific policy and governance (cost-allocation tagging, spend guardrails) is enforced</td><td>⚠️ Partial — <code>$.tags[*]</code>, <code>Management/PolicyAssignments</code> are generic governance signals, not FinOps-specific enforcement</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M05</td><td>Invoices are reconciled and cross-charged (chargeback/showback) to internal teams</td><td>❌ Not collected — same billing-hierarchy gap <code>caf.billing.yaml</code>&#39;s misnaming note documents (EA/MCA enrollment, invoice sections)</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M06</td><td>The FinOps practice&#39;s own maturity is periodically reassessed</td><td>❌ Organisational — this is the meta-capability describing running assessments like this one</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M07</td><td><strong>Automation, Tools &amp; Services</strong> — FinOps tools, automation and services are selected and integrated to fit organizational needs</td><td>❌ Organisational/tooling choice</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M08</td><td><strong>Intersecting Disciplines</strong> — FinOps practices are aligned with intersecting disciplines (ITAM, ITSM, security, sustainability)</td><td>❌ Organisational</td></tr><tr><td>FINOPS-M09</td><td><strong>Executive Strategy Alignment</strong> <em>(new in the 2026 framework)</em> — FinOps informs executive priorities, multi-year investment strategy, product prioritisation and strategic decision support</td><td>❌ Organisational — manual rule</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="what-this-means-for-the-rule-file" tabindex="-1">What this means for the rule file <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-this-means-for-the-rule-file" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;What this means for the rule file&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>src/assess/rules/finops.review.yaml</code> holds <strong>23 rules</strong>: the 22 Microsoft Learn capabilities plus <code>FINOPS-M09</code>. Of these, 7 are automated (U01, U04, Q02, Q03, O02, O03, O04), and 16 are manual (U02, U03, Q01, Q04, Q05, O01, O05, M01–M09). The Manage domain (9 capabilities) is close to a hard floor — it is organisational, and even tagging/policy gives only generic governance data, not FinOps-specific signal. The more consequential finding is upstream of any rule file: <strong><code>Get-ScoutCostInventory</code> is gated behind an opt-in module Scout deliberately does not install</strong>, so <code>FINOPS-U01</code> and <code>FINOPS-U04</code> — the &quot;Understand usage and cost&quot; domain&#39;s automated half, which every other Optimize/Quantify capability ultimately depends on — only score in an environment where an operator has separately installed <code>Az.CostManagement</code>; without it they report NotAssessed, never a scored zero.</p>',32)])])}const m=e(n,[["render",s]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
